<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#brak">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brak</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brak was the title of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waalo">Waalo</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> kingdom on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> river. The Brak was chosen by a council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> from among the royal maternal lineages and ruled from Nder, sharing power with titled officials and royal women such as the linger, the queen mother or a royal sister. The title ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed Waalo in 1855.</p></div>
